# The vendored LiveKit SDK is checked against upstream by its sha256 (the hash
# is in the doc comment on LIVEKIT_JS in client/src/app.rs). With
# core.autocrlf=true — the default on Windows — a checkout would rewrite its two
# newlines to CRLF, so the file on disk would no longer match the published one
# and `include_str!` would compile in something two bytes off depending on who
# cloned it. `-text` turns that off for this file only. Nothing here is about
# JavaScript being newline-sensitive; it is about the hash staying checkable.
client/assets/livekit-client.umd.js -text
